<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help: </ansi><ansi fg="command">Special Moves & Cooldown</ansi>

Several combat abilities are considered <ansi fg="yellow-bold">special moves</ansi> and share a common
cooldown. Triggering any one of them puts all of them on cooldown for the
same window.

<ansi fg="yellow">Special moves that share this cooldown:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">bash</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">grapple</ansi>
              - Melee control moves: stagger, disorient, knock down, restrain.
  <ansi fg="command">taunt</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">warcry</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">rally</ansi>
              - Shouts and rallying cries; the voice spends from the
                same well of focus.
  <ansi fg="command">throw</ansi>     - Hurling a grenade or other throwable item.
  <ansi fg="command">cast</ansi>      - Starting most spells. Spells that summon a helper out
              of nothing use their own, longer recovery instead.
  <ansi fg="command">consider</ansi>  - Sizes up a fight. Uses your special-move recovery.
              See <ansi fg="command">help consider</ansi>.
  <ansi fg="command">fire</ansi>      - Every shot starts the cooldown, so a shot leaves your
              other special moves recovering. A spent cooldown never
              stops a shot, or an ambush shot. See <ansi fg="command">help fire</ansi>.
  <ansi fg="command">attack</ansi>    - Only when you engage from hiding. That opening blow is
              an ambush and spends the cooldown. Ordinary swings do not.
              See <ansi fg="command">help ambush</ansi>.
  <ansi fg="command">gore</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">maul</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">rake</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">pounce</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">throttle</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">drain</ansi>
              - Natural-weapon moves for bodies shaped to use them.
  Mutation abilities (<ansi fg="command">venom-coat</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">cocoon</ansi>) share it too.
  The <ansi fg="command">kick</ansi> variants <ansi fg="command">stomp</ansi> and <ansi fg="command">knee</ansi>, and <ansi fg="command">tailsweep</ansi> for <ansi fg="command">trip</ansi>,
  are the same moves under another name.

Submissions (chokes, joint locks) fire automatically when you
have dominant control in a grapple; no command needed. See
<ansi fg="command">help submission</ansi>.

<ansi fg="yellow">Why shared cooldown?</ansi>

These moves represent bursts of focused effort. The body and mind need a
moment to recover before another such effort can be made. You can still
attack normally between special moves.

Physical moves spend Stamina; rhetoric moves spend Conviction. Carried load
raises physical prices, while each move's governing skill lowers its price.
These voluntary actions require full payment and refuse before consuming their
cooldown, item, ammunition, combat round, or effect.

<ansi fg="yellow">Checking cooldowns:</ansi>

  Use <ansi fg="command">cooldowns</ansi> to see all active cooldowns, including how many rounds
  remain before your next special move is available.

